mainmenu "Atlas upstream host tests (built from tapeout-chipyard)"

config ATLAS_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_S
	int "Watchdog: seconds of wall time before the test is declared hung"
	default 120
	help
	  Upstream polls the Atlas status register up to 200 million times before
	  reporting a failure, which takes minutes on a slow link, and some tests
	  have no timeout. The shim runs the test's main() in the main thread
	  and a watchdog thread that, after this many seconds, writes
	  execControl=0 (stops Atlas), prints "ATLASUP <test> TIMEOUT" and ends
	  the run with exit code 124.

	  It cannot help if a bus access never returns; the last line printed
	  before the hang then names the stage.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
